#
# Unattended imports with diaspora: add with `crontab -e`, after copying
# diaspora-cron (next to this file) to ~/bin and editing what it exports.
#
# cron mails what a job prints.  `diaspora auto --cron` prints nothing when
# there is nothing to import; otherwise one line per planned commit (applied,
# adapted, failed, ...), whether the plan stopped and why, and its log file
# (the full output, in ~/.cache/diaspora/<repo>-<hash>/auto/).
MAILTO=me@example.org

# m  h  dom mon dow  command
# Every night at 01:30: VACASK, then xyce (one at a time: each runs its full
# regression for every stage).
30 1 * * *  $HOME/bin/diaspora-cron VACASK xyce

# The repositories with the long regressions, on Saturday mornings.
0 6 * * 6   $HOME/bin/diaspora-cron nvc iverilog

# A single repository, without the script (when the tests need nothing from
# your login environment), and smaller stages:
# 30 2 * * *  cd /usr/local/src/VACASK && /usr/local/bin/diaspora auto --cron --stage-size 4

# Only show the plan each Monday (cron mails it), import nothing:
# 0 8 * * 1  /usr/local/bin/diaspora -C VACASK auto --dry-run --no-fetch
